					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This was fun. Not hard to read or emotionally taxing, which was good for this specific media in my opinion, and rather charming as a whole tale. I don't like the idea of a Foundation employing such humanized artificial intelligence because of the liabilities such humanization poses, but it's not a bad product as a piece of fiction. Thus, I upvote.</p> <p>&#8230; I'd still have upvoted without the smilies, though.</p> 
				 	]]>
